# Grafana Deployment on Kubernetes – Nautilus DevOps Lab

## Project Overview

The Nautilus DevOps team required Grafana to be deployed on a Kubernetes cluster to collect and analyze application analytics.

The objective was to deploy Grafana using a Kubernetes Deployment and expose the application externally through a NodePort service.

The deployment was successfully created, the Grafana pod reached the Running state, and the login page was verified with an HTTP 200 OK response.

## Objectives

- Deploy Grafana on the Kubernetes cluster.
- Create a Deployment named `grafana-deployment-nautilus`.
- Use a Grafana container image.
- Expose Grafana through a NodePort service.
- Configure NodePort `32000`.
- Verify the Grafana application and login page.

