## 1. Create the Grafana Deployment

The Grafana deployment was created using the official Grafana Docker image.

### Command

```bash
kubectl create deployment grafana-deployment-nautilus \
  --image=grafana/grafana:latest
```

### Terminal Output

```text
deployment.apps/grafana-deployment-nautilus created
```

The deployment instructs Kubernetes to run the Grafana application inside a container.

## 2. Create the NodePort Service

A NodePort service was created to expose Grafana on port 32000.

### Command

```bash
kubectl expose deployment grafana-deployment-nautilus \
  --name=grafana-service-nautilus \
  --type=NodePort \
  --port=3000 \
  --target-port=3000
```

### Terminal Output

```text
service/grafana-service-nautilus exposed
```

The service initially receives an automatically assigned NodePort.

The following command sets the required NodePort to 32000.

```bash
kubectl patch service grafana-service-nautilus \
  -p '{"spec":{"ports":[{"port":3000,"targetPort":3000,"nodePort":32000}]}}'
```

### Terminal Output

```text
service/grafana-service-nautilus patched
```

