## 5. Verify the Grafana Login Page

The Grafana login endpoint was tested from inside the Kubernetes cluster using a temporary curl container.

### Command

```bash
kubectl run grafana-test --rm -i --restart=Never \
  --image=curlimages/curl -- \
  curl -I http://grafana-service-nautilus:3000/login
```

### Actual HTTP Response

```text
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Cache-Control: no-store
Content-Type: text/html; charset=UTF-8
X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
X-Frame-Options: deny
Date: Sun, 01 Nov 2026 10:30:39 GMT
```

The temporary test pod was automatically deleted after the test completed.

```text
pod "grafana-test" deleted from default namespace
```

**Verification result:** HTTP 200 OK confirmed that Grafana's login page was responding successfully through the Kubernetes service.

## 6. Application Access

Grafana listens on container port 3000.

The Kubernetes NodePort exposes the application on port 32000.

